  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Mark Recovery Program (Canada)",
  "description": "Mark Recovery Program (Canada) Measurement Details Coded-wire tagged and/or adipose-clipped Chinook, coho, pink, sockeye, chum and steelhead are sampled for age, sexual maturity, length, weight and color for stock composition, exploitation and survival rates, hatchery contribution and run-timing. Geographic Area Coastal British Columbia Other Comments Data are complete for Chinook and coho from 1975, steelhead from 1976, and chum from 1979. Pink and sockeye data are intermittent back to 1984 and 1978, respectively. [ A TCODE project ]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.",
